imary hip-flexion contributor and remains active during the controlled lowering phase as the hips extend toward the hanging position. The eccentric action is conventional and the bottom position does not impose unusually severe loaded stretch, so only a mild recovery premium is warranted.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 102.23, "tension_fraction": 0.6459, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 66.03, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["high_relative_tension", "controlled_eccentric_hip_extension", "conventional_contractile_fatigue"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "mild"}, {"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "rectus_femoris", "rationale": "Rectus femoris contributes dynamically to hip flexion at moderate relative tension. Although it lengthens across the hip during the lowering phase, the maintained knee extension shortens it across the knee and limits extreme whole-muscle length. The resulting loading profile remains close to conventional dynamic reference.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 91.44, "tension_fraction": 0.3741, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "moderate", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 34.21, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["conventional_dynamic_hip_flexion"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "mild"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "Oblique activity is predominantly continuous lumbopelvic and anti-rotation stabilization rather than substantial loaded dynamic rotation. The exposure can contribute to acute fatigue but lacks a strong mechanism for persistent local force impairment per unit tension.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "tensi