ation", "muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "high", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "moderate", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "scapulothoracic_articulation", "rationale": "As the arm elevates, the scapula must upwardly rotate and remain controlled against the thorax. Serratus anterior and trapezial musculature generate substantial force to coordinate scapulohumeral rhythm and transmit load from the upper limb into the trunk. The unilateral cable configuration also increases scapular control requirements compared with a bilaterally guided machine.", "load_exposure": 0.5200, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "muscle_force_transmission", "rotation", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "moderate", "stabilization_requirement": "high", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "acromioclavicular_joint", "rationale": "The AC joint transmits force between the clavicle and scapula while the scapula upwardly rotates during arm elevation. The lateral-raise arc creates meaningful shoulder-girdle rotational demand and load transmission, although the AC joint remains secondary to the glenohumeral and scapulothoracic components.", "load_exposure": 0.3400, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["rotation", "muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "moderate", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "radiocarpal_joint", "rationale": "The wrist mainly transmits handle force while maintaining a near-neutral position. Forearm musculature provides modest stabilization, but there is little direct wrist flexion, extension, or deviation moment.", "load_exposure": 0.1200, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}, {"joint": "elbow_joint", "rationale": "The elbow remains slightly flexed and largely fixed throughout the movement. It mainly serves as a rigid link transmitting cable force to the shoulder, with little direct flexion-extension moment or local muscular loading.", "load_exposure": 0.0800, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["stabilization", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "minimal", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "glenohumeral_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
