", "rationale": "Maintains glenohumeral centring continuously during the hang, but at low force relative to its large available capacity, with no active lengthening under meaningful load. Sustained low-level isometry of this kind produces intra-set fatigue that largely resolves on release rather than a persistent force deficit, so it sits slightly below the dynamic reference despite its continuous duty cycle.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "tension_fraction": 0.0293, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 5.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "sustained", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_sustained_stabilizing_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Grip tension is genuinely continuous throughout the hang with no unloading phase, and sustained gripping does materially restrict local perfusion. This raises it above the sub-reference value assigned to briefly-gripping exercises, but the fatigue generated by sustained submaximal gripping recovers substantially once tension is released, so the neutral reference rather than an elevated value is appropriate.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "tension_fraction": 0.0735, "perfusion_constraint": "moderate", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 4.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "sustained", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["sustained_gripping_isometric_tension_with_partial_perfusion_constraint"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "rationale": "Provides intra-abdominal bracing at low force with no contractile lengthening under 