revis", "rationale": "Produces substantial hip-adduction force and stabilizes the femoral head and pelvis while the supported leg bears the lateral body load. The supplied value already captures its complete high-tension isometric contribution.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 66.55, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission", "joint_stabilization"], "tension_fraction": 0.6545, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 43.56, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 43.56, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "Produces the lateral trunk and pelvic stabilization required to keep the body aligned while resisting gravity-induced side bending and axial rotation. The supplied value already combines the ipsilateral anti-lateral-flexion and bilateral anti-rotation force state.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "antagonist_co_contraction"], "tension_fraction": 0.3740, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 30.56, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 30.56, "input_contribution_classification": "mixed_propulsive_and_stabilizing"}, {"muscle": "gluteus_medius", "rationale": "Stabilizes the pelvis and femoral head in the frontal plane while the adductors maintain the elevated side-plank position. The modest allocation reflects complementary pelvic control rather than primary force production.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 113.75, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "limb_position_maintenance", "isometric_fixation", "multi_joint_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.0352, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 4.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "rationale": "Provides circumferential abdominal stiffness and transfers force between the shoulder girdle, pelvis, and supported leg without allowing trunk deformation.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.1365, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "rationale": "Maintains ribcage-to-pelvis alignment and limits lumbar extension while the obliques resist lateral flexion and rotation.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "antagonist_co_contraction"], "tension_fraction": 0.1029, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "Centres the humeral head of the supporting arm while bodyweight is transmitted through the shoulder. Forearm and bench support keep the required cuff fraction relatively low.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0146, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "serratus_anterior", "rationale": "Maintains scapular contact with the thorax and supports load transfer through the planted forearm and shoulder.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.03, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0555, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "deltoid_lateral", "rationale": "Contributes low-level shoulder-abduction and compression force to maintain the supporting upper arm beneath the torso.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 45.73, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0328, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "erector_spinae", "rationale": "Co-contracts with the abdominal wall to maintain neutral spinal alignment and prevent flexion or rotation during the side-plank hold.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 106.48, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "antagonist_co_contraction", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0141, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "gluteus_minimus", "rationale": "Provides low-level femoral-head and pelvic stabilization alongside the gluteus medius while the adductors bear the principal load.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.82, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "limb_position_maintenance", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0483, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.20, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "triceps_lateral_head", "rationale": "Maintains the supporting elbow position and transfers force through the upper arm, although forearm support substantially reduces elbow-extension demand.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.10, "mechanical_roles": ["isometric_fixation", "load_transmission", "limb_position_maintenance"], "tension_fraction": 0.0277, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}], "saturated_muscles": [], "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled isometric hold", "execution_scope": "bilateral", "range_of_motion": "full intended hold position", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}, "tension_expansion_ratio": 1.1460, "propulsive_vector_sum_cm2": 131.52, "propulsive_fcsa_demand_cm2": 131.52, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 150.72}	{"obliques": 25.98, "rotator_cuffs": 2.00, "erector_spinae": 1.20, "gluteus_medius": 3.40, "adductor_magnus": 51.66, "deltoid_lateral": 1.28, "gluteus_minimus": 1.02, "rectus_abdominis": 2.13, "serratus_anterior": 1.70, "transverse_abdominis": 2.40, "triceps_lateral_head": 0.85, "adductor_longus_brevis": 39.20}	{"slug": "copenhagen_plank", "notes": ["The adductor groups receive the highest modifiers because they sustain unusually high, well-aligned force at useful muscle lengths, although the absence of dynamic ROM keeps them below the neutral dynamic reference.", "The obliques and most secondary stabilizers receive 0.85 because their tension is sustained but predominantly isometric.", "The transverse abdominis, rotator cuffs, and erector spinae receive the minimum modifier because their exposure consists almost entirely of low-ROM bracing or joint stabilization.", "No muscle receives a modifier above 0.90 because the Copenhagen plank is an isometric exercise without meaningful loaded concentric-eccentric excursion.", "ETU values equal active tension exposure multiplied by the listed H_m values within rounding tolerance."], "etu_sum_cm2": 132.82, "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"H_m": 0.9000, "muscle": "adductor_magnus", "etu_cm2": 51.66, "rationale": "High, sustained, well-aligned adductor tension merits a modifier above ordinary stabilization, but the predominantly isometric contraction and absent loaded ROM keep it below the dynamic reference.", "normalized_etu": 0.4910, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 105.22, "smh_interpretation": "The supported hip is held in a demanding adduction position while the muscle sustains a large fraction of bodyweight, but there is negligible concentric-eccentric excursion.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 57.40, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 0.9000, "muscle": "adductor_longus_brevis", "etu_cm2": 39.20, "rationale": "The exercise provides unusually high and specific isometric adductor loading, supporting a modestly elevated stabilizer modifier without equating it to full-ROM dynamic adduction.", "normalized_etu": 0.5890, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 66.55, "smh_interpretation": "The adductors sustain high force at a useful hip position while supporting the pelvis, but do not shorten or lengthen through a substantial resisted range.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 43.56, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "obliques", "etu_cm2": 25.98, "rationale": "The trunk demand is substantial and sustained but remains predominantly isometric and lacks productive shortening-lengthening excursion.", "normalized_etu": 0.3180, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "smh_interpretation": "The obliques sustain substantial anti-lateral-flexion and anti-rotation force while trunk geometry remains nearly fixed.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 30.56, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscl