ion against the cable's pull rather than moving through a range; the force required is low and the muscle is held near a shortened-to-neutral length, so its fatigue is largely transient.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 30.46, "tension_fraction": 0.2042, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "moderate", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 6.22, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "moderate", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_positional_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Grips the handle at submaximal force with no lengthening under load and no meaningful perfusion restriction; such fatigue resolves rapidly once tension is released.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "tension_fraction": 0.1000, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 5.44, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_gripping_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "Maintains glenohumeral centring in the extended-shoulder position at very low force relative to its large available capacity, without lengthening under meaningful load; persistent local deficit is minimal.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "tension_fraction": 0.0293, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 5.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "moderate", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_stabilizing_isometric_ten