g this exercise near the high end of conventional direct elbow-flexion loading.", "load_exposure": 0.7800, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "radiocarpal_joint", "rationale": "The wrist must stabilize and transmit the dumbbell load while maintaining a largely neutral or slightly extended position. Grip and forearm co-contraction generate meaningful radiocarpal force transmission, but there is little intended wrist motion or large direct wrist moment.", "load_exposure": 0.1800, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "glenohumeral_joint", "rationale": "The upper arm is externally supported by the preacher bench, substantially removing dynamic shoulder motion and stabilization requirements. Some proximal force transmission occurs through the biceps and other tissues crossing the shoulder, but glenohumeral loading remains low relative to unsupported curling variants.", "load_exposure": 0.1000, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "minimal", "stabilization_requirement": "minimal", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "elbow_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
