 substantially lengthened wrist-extension position.", "The modifier remains below the upper calibration range because the dumbbell resistance profile still varies with wrist and implement geometry and does not represent specialized eccentric overload.", "The wrist extensors receive the minimum modifier because their exposure consists primarily of antagonist stabilization and movement reversal.", "Forearm-orientation and proximal forearm contributions receive reduced modifiers because they are predominantly isometric and low-ROM.", "ETU values equal active tension exposure multiplied by the listed H_m values within rounding tolerance."], "etu_sum_cm2": 58.90, "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"H_m": 1.1000, "muscle": "wrist_flexors", "etu_cm2": 55.77, "rationale": "Near-maximal recruitment, stable forearm support, controlled eccentric loading, broad isolated ROM, and substantial tension in the lengthened wrist-extension position justify a clear positive modifier.", "normalized_etu": 1.0252, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric", "isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "broad", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "smh_interpretation": "The wrists descend into substantial extension under dumbbell load, lengthening the wrist flexors before they flex the wrists through the available supported range. Finger flexion also remains active to retain the implements.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 50.70, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "substantially_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 0.8000, "muscle": "wrist_extensors", "etu_cm2": 1.60, "rationale": "Low-level antagonist co-contraction and joint stabilization with negligible productive extension ROM warrant the lower calibration anchor.", "normalized_etu": 0.0298, "contraction_mode": ["isometric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.67, "smh_interpretation": "The wrist extensors primarily regulate joint position and reversal without directly resisted wrist-extension work through a productive range.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "poor", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "pronators_supinators", "etu_cm2": 0.85, "rationale": "Forearm-orientation maintenance is mechanically necessary but predominantly isometric and low-ROM.", "normalized_etu": 0.0140, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 60.88, "smh_interpretation": "The forearms remain supinated without directly resisted pronation or supination through meaningful ROM.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "brachioradialis", "etu_cm2": 0.68, "rationale": "The exposure is low-level, positional, and predominantly isometric.", "normalized_etu": 0.0606, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 11.22, "smh_interpretation": "The elbow and proximal forearm remain nearly fixed while external support removes most dynamic demand.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 0.80, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}], "modifier_distribution": {"mode": 0.8500, "median": 0.8500, "maximum": 1.1000, "minimum": 0.8000, "unweighted_mean": 0.9000, "tension_weighted_mean": 1.0807}, "hypertrophic_quality_ratio": 1.0807, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 54.50}	{"wrist_flexors": 1.0000, "brachioradialis": 0.9500, "wrist_extensors": 0.9500, "pronators_supinators": 0.9500}	{"slug": "seated_dumbbell_wrist_curl", "notes": ["The prime mover sits at the neutral reference through offsetting factors rather than an absence of features: near-maximal relative tension and end-range loaded lengthening push upward, while very brief meaningful tension and low absolute force in a short-range isolation push downward.", "The very high tension fraction was deliberately not converted into a modifier on its own, since load magnitude is already carried by Active Tension Exposure and the specification warns against assigning a large R_m solely for high tension fraction.", "Wrist extensors were held at 0.95 despite lengthening during wrist flexion, because they are co-contracting antagonists at low force rather than resisting the load at long length.", "The intense acute burning typical of direct forearm work was excluded as a target variable; it resolves quickly and does not represent persistent restoration of force-producing readiness.", "This exercise was kept at the same prime-mover value as the palms-down wrist extension, since no identifiable mechanism distinguishes their persistent recovery profiles."], "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Two factors offset here. The near-maximal tension fraction of 0.93 would ordinarily support a small positive modifier for the nonlinear residual cost of operating close to available capacity, and the forearm resting on a bench with the wrist free does keep meaningful resistance present as the wrist extends into a lengthened position. Against this, the movement is a very short-range isolation with brief meaningful tension per repetition and low absolute forces relative to the group's structural tolerance, which the calibration scale treats as a sub-reference feature. With one factor pointing up and one down, the neutral reference is the correct holistic estimate.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "tension_fraction": 0.9320, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "very_high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 50.70, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "brief", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["conventional_contractile_fatigue", "near_maximal_relative_tension_nonlinear_residual"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "mild"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "wrist_extensors", "rationale": "Acts as a low-force antagonist providing wrist joint stability; although it is lengthened as the wrist flexes, it is not resisting the load, so no high-force lengthening applies and its brief tension leaves little persistent deficit.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.67, "tension_fraction": 0.0373, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "brief", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_antagonist_co_contraction"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "pronators_supinators", "rationale": "Holds the supinated forearm position against the bench at very low force with no dynamic rotation under load; the fatigue produced is transient.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 60.88, "tension_fraction": 0.0164, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "brief", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_stabilizing_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "brachioradialis", "rationale": "Contributes minimal elbow stabilization with the forearm supported on the bench; no excursion or loaded lengthening occurs, so persistent recovery cost per unit tension falls just below reference.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 11.22, "tension_fraction": 0.0713, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 0.80, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "brief", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["low_level_stabilizing_isometric_tension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}], "modifier_distribution": {"mode": 0.9500, "median": 0.9500, "maximum": 1.0000, "minimum": 0.9500, "unweighted_mean": 0.9625, "tension_weighted_mean": 0.9982}, "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 54.50}	{"elbow_joint": 0.1000, "radiocarpal_joint": 0.8400}	{"slug": "seated_dumbbell_wrist_curl", "notes": ["This is a highly localized wrist-flexion exercise with minimal proximal-joint involvement because the forearms are supported.", "The radiocarpal score is slightly higher than the corresponding palms-down wrist-extension variant because the larger 24 kg working load produces greater direct wrist moment and flexor-force transmission under the same supported geometry."], "loaded_joints": ["radiocarpal_joint", "elbow_joint"], "reconciliation": "PASS", "joint_evaluation": [{"joint": "radiocarpal_joint", "rationale": "The radiocarpal joint is the primary loaded articulation. With the forearms supported and the dumbbells acting through the hands, the resistance creates a direct wrist-extension moment that must be opposed by the wrist flexors. The relatively large external hand moment arm and high flexor force generated through short internal moment arms produce substantial joint reaction and compression. Full intended ROM also exposes the wrist to meaningful loading in extension and flexion. Relative to conventional wrist-loading exercises, a 24 kg bilateral working load places this exercise near the high end of direct wrist-flexion mechanical exposure.", "load_exposure": 0.8400, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "muscle_force_transmission", "loaded_end_range"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "very_high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "very_high"}, {"joint": "elbow_joint", "rationale": "The elbows remain effectively fixed while the forearms are externally supported, so little elbow flexion or extension moment is required. Forearm flexor forces are transmitted proximally and create minor elbow-region mechanical exposure, but the elbow is not a meaningful load-bearing articulation in the exercise.", "load_exposure": 0.1000, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "minimal", "stabilization_requirement": "minimal", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "radiocarpal_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
side_facing_reverse_pec_deck	20.00	108.17	{"obliques": 12.34, "rhomboids": 16.53, "brachialis": 4.63, "rotator_cuffs": 14.71, "biceps_brachii": 3.42, "erector_spinae": 6.28, "trapezius_lower": 7.19, "trapezius_upper": 3.71, "trapezius_middle": 16.90, "deltoid_posterior": 17.66, "serratus_anterior": 2.27, "transverse_abdominis": 2.53}	{"obliques": 12.34, "rhomboids": 16.53, "brachialis": 4.63, "teres_major": 1.50, "rotator_cuffs": 14.71, "wrist_flexors": 5.00, "biceps_brachii": 3.42, "erector_spinae": 6.28, "deltoid_lateral": 8.00, "trapezius_lower": 7.19, "trapezius_upper": 3.71, "latissimus_dorsi": 5.00, "rectus_abdominis": 2.00, "trapezius_middle": 16.90, "deltoid_posterior": 17.66, "serratus_anterior": 2.27, "pronators_supinators": 3.00, "transverse_abdominis": 2.53}	{"slug": "side_facing_reverse_pec_deck", "notes": ["Supplied vector sums to 108.17, matching systemic_propulsive_fcsa_demand exactly.", "The supplied vector contained brachialis and biceps_brachii, which cannot be propulsive in a fixed-elbow fly. Per the input-handling rules their values were retained as an established lower bound of active tension and reclassified as isometric load transmission rather than removed. This is recorded as an inconsistency in the naming of the previous model's output, not an arithmetic error.", "The large obliques and erector_spinae entries are consistent with the side-facing single-arm geometry, which converts the resistance into a sustained unilateral trunk rotation moment. No increase was applied because the supplied values already appear to represent that full demand.", "Six muscles were added, all along specific pathways absent from the supplied vector: lateral deltoid torque past the frontal plane, lat and teres major transverse extension, grip and forearm rotation control, and anterior trunk bracing.", "Tension expansion ratio of 1.2265 is modest, reflecting a seat-supported machine in which the trunk demand was already largely captured by the previous model.", "Pectoralis major and anterior deltoid were considered as antagonists but excluded; their activity during a controlled reverse fly is incidental rather than mechanically required, which does not meet the evidence standard.", "load_capacity_kg of 20 is read as the total bilateral-convention load for this single-arm exercise. It was not used to recalculate any mechanical value, since the supplied vector is authoritative."], "added_muscles": ["deltoid_lateral", "latissimus_dorsi", "wrist_flexors", "pronators_supinators", "rectus_abdominis", "teres_major"], "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"muscle": "deltoid_posterior", "rationale": "Prime mover for glenohumeral horizontal abduction against the pad or handle. Supplied value retained; no additional mechanical demand exists beyond the torque already accounted for.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.65, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.7165, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 17.66, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 17.66, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "trapezius_middle", "rationale": "Produces scapular retraction, which is a task-relevant component of the movement rather than mere fixation. Retraction torque and scapular stabilization are one force state here, so the supplied value is retained without addition.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 26.18, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "scapular_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.6455, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 16.90, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 16.90, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "rhomboids", "rationale": "Retraction with downward rotation contribution, working through a genuine scapular excursion. Supplied value retained.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 28.25, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "scapular_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.5851, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 16.53, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 16.53, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "Infraspinatus and teres minor contribute directly to horizontal abduction and external rotation while the whole cuff centres the humeral head against the distraction created by the lateral handle pull. Both roles are expressed by a single force state, so no increase is applied on top of the supplied value.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "joint_stabilization"], "tension_fraction": 0.0861, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 14.71, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 14.71, "input_contribution_classification": "mixed_propulsive_and_stabilizing"}, {"muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "In the side-facing single-arm configuration the resistance vector acts unilaterally in the transverse plane, generating a continuous trunk rotation moment toward the machine. The obliques resist that rotation isometrically. The comparatively high supplied value is mechanically sound for this setup and is retained as the complete tension estimate.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.1510, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 12.34, "contraction_character": ["isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 12.34, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "deltoid_lateral", "rationale": "Added because the posterior fibres of the lateral deltoid lie behind the glenohumeral axis of horizontal abduction and contribute measurable torque once the arm passes the frontal plane, while the whole head also supports the abducted arm position against gravity. The previous model appears to have attributed the entire deltoid demand to the posterior head.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 45.73, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "limb_position_maintenance"], "tension_fraction": 0.1749, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 8.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "trapezius_lower", "rationale": "Contributes to retraction while opposing the scapular elevation tendency generated by upper trapezius and by the handle line of pull. Supplied value already reflects both; retained.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 14.98, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.4800, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 7.19, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 7.19, "input_contribution_classification": "mixed_propulsive_and_stabilizing"}, {"muscle": "erector_spinae", "rationale": "Works with the obliques to hold the spine against the unilateral rotation and lateral flexion moment. Extensor tension also prevents the thoracic flexion that would otherwise accompany the pull. Retained at the supplied value.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 106.48, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0590, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 6.28, "contraction_character": ["isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 6.28, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "latissimus_dorsi", "rationale": "Added because at the abducted arm position the lat contributes a transverse extension component and resists humeral distraction at the glenohumeral joint. Magnitude kept modest since its moment arm for horizontal abduction is small at this arm height.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 43.85, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "joint_stabilization"], "tension_fraction": 0.1140, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 5.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Added because the entire resistance is transmitted through the hand on the handle. Grip force is the necessary link in the kinetic chain and was absent from the supplied vector.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "mechanical_roles": ["grip_maintenance", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.0919, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 5.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "brachialis", "rationale": "The elbow angle is fixed throughout a reverse fly, so this muscle produces no task-relevant elbow torque and cannot be propulsive despite its position in the supplied vector. Its force isometrically maintains the elbow angle and transmits handle reaction force from forearm to humerus. The supplied value is retained as the mandated lower bound and reclassified rather than removed.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 44.05, "mechanical_roles": ["isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.1051, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 4.63, "contraction_character": ["isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 4.63, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "trapezius_upper", "rationale": "Supports the shoulder girdle and assists upward rotation while the arm is held at shoulder height. Low-excursion positional tension; retained at the supplied value.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 19.36, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.1916, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 3.71, "contraction_character": ["isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.71, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "biceps_brachii", "rationale": "As with brachialis, no elbow torque is produced as task output. The long head additionally resists anterior humeral head translation at the glenohumeral joint. Supplied value retained and reclassified as isometric load transmission.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 39.81, "mechanical_roles": ["isometric_fixation", "load_transmission", "joint_stabilization"], "tension_fraction": 0.0859, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 3.42, "contraction_character": ["isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.42, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "pronators_supinators", "rationale": "Added because the handle applies a rotational moment about the forearm long axis that must be resisted to keep the grip orientation constant through the arc. Small magnitude, specific pathway.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 60.88, "mechanical_roles": ["limb_position_maintenance", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0493, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "rationale": "Generates intra-abdominal pressure supporting the anti-rotation demand carried mainly by the obliques. Retained at supplied value.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing"], "tension_fraction": 0.1152, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 2.53, "contraction_character": ["isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.53, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "serratus_anterior", "rationale": "As a protractor it is antagonist to the primary retraction action; its low-level tension keeps the scapula against the thorax and contributes upward rotation so the glenoid tracks the moving humerus. Correctly small in the supplied vector; retained.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.03, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "antagonist_co_contraction"], "tension_fraction": 0.0630, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 2.27, "contraction_character": ["co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.27, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "rationale": "Added as the anterior partner to erector spinae in maintaining a rigid trunk cylinder against the rotational load. Deliberately small, since the oblique and transverse abdominal contributions carry the specific anti-rotation demand.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing"], "tension_fraction": 0.0823, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "teres_major", "rationale": "Added as a small synergist to latissimus dorsi in transverse extension and humeral head stabilization. Its tension fraction is relatively high only because its maximum FCSA is very small.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 4.50, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "joint_stabilization"], "tension_fraction": 0.3333, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}], "saturated_muscles": [], "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}, "tension_expansion_ratio": 1.2265, "propulsive_vector_sum_cm2": 108.17, "propulsive_fcsa_demand_cm2": 108.17, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 132.67}	{"obliques": 10.49, "rhomboids": 15.70, "brachialis": 3.94, "teres_major": 1.35, "rotator_cuffs": 13.97, "wrist_flexors": 4.25, "biceps_brachii": 2.91, "erector_spinae": 5.34, "deltoid_lateral": 7.60, "trapezius_lower": 6.47, "trapezius_upper": 3.15, "latissimus_dorsi": 4.50, "rectus_abdominis": 1.70, "trapezius_middle": 16.06, "deltoid_posterior": 18.54, "serratus_anterior": 1.93, "pronators_supinators": 2.55, "transverse_abdominis": 2.15}	{"slug": "side_facing_reverse_pec_deck", "notes": ["No muscle received the 0.80 floor. Every included muscle either performs dynamic work or carries meaningful sustained load, so none meets the description of incidental co-contraction or trivial postural fixation.", "Only deltoid_posterior exceeds 1.00, and only by one step, on the strength of the extended cross-body start position that the single-arm side-facing configuration allows.", "The scapular retractors are deliberately separated from the posterior deltoid at 0.95: they reach peak demand at their shortest length over a small excursion, which is the opposite length profile to the working humerus.", "Hypertrophic quality ratio of 0.9241 is below the global target of approximately 1.00, driven by the large number of low-excursion isometric entries the mechanical model required. The tension-weighted figure sits well above the unweighted mean of 0.8917 because the near-reference dynamic muscles carry most of the tension.", "Normalized ETU reaches 0.7521 for posterior deltoid and 0.6134 for middle trapezius, the only muscles approaching a substantial share of a full reference effective-repetition equivalent.", "Teres major shows a normalized ETU of 0.3000 despite the smallest absolute tension in the vector; this is an artefact of its very small maximum FCSA and should not be read as a large stimulus."], "etu_sum_cm2": 122.60, "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"H_m": 1.0500, "muscle": "deltoid_posterior", "etu_cm2": 18.54, "rationale": "The single-arm side-facing setup permits the arm to travel further across the body at the start than a chest-supported bilateral version, loading the posterior deltoid in a modestly lengthened position. Resistance is present from the first degrees of the arc rather than appearing only near retraction. Bonus limited to 1.05 because the cam still delivers appreciable torque demand at the shortened end and the arc is short in absolute terms.", "normalized_etu": 0.7521, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.65, "smh_interpretation": "No SMH factor supplied. The starting position places the humerus across the midline with the posterior deltoid at meaningful length under load, which supports a small bonus but not a large one.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 17.66, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "trapezius_middle", "etu_cm2": 16.06, "rationale": "Peak retraction demand coincides with maximum scapular adduction, the shortest position for this muscle, and total scapular excursion is small relative to the arm's arc. Reduced modestly to 0.95 for shortened bias with limited high-tension ROM; it stays near reference because the contraction is genuinely dynamic and well loaded.", "normalized_etu": 0.6134, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "limited", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 26.18, "smh_interpretation": "Scapular retractors are shortest exactly where the machine demands most torque, so no stretch-mediated case exists.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 16.90, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "shortened"}, {"H_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "rhomboids", "etu_cm2": 15.70, "rationale": "Shares the retraction length profile: highest demand at end-range adduction where the muscle is shortest, over a small excursion. 0.95.", "normalized_etu": 0.5558, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "limited", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 28.25, "smh_interpretation": "Same shortened-at-peak profile as middle trapezius.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 16.53, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "shortened"}, {"H_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "etu_cm2": 13.97, "rationale": "Placed above the pure stabilizer band because a genuine dynamic external rotation and horizontal abduction component exists, not merely positional fixation. Held below reference at 0.95 because a substantial share of the tension is centring isometry with little excursion.", "normalized_etu": 0.0818, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric", "isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "smh_interpretation": "The external rotators shorten through the movement while the anterior cuff lengthens, giving no net length advantage across the group.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 14.71, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "obliques", "etu_cm2": 10.49, "rationale": "The tension is meaningful and sustained rather than incidental, which places it above the floor, but it is isometric with essentially no muscle excursion. 0.85 per the standard treatment of meaningful low-ROM stabilization.", "normalized_etu": 0.1284, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "smh_interpretation": "Anti-rotation work holds a fixed mid-range length; no lengthened loading.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 12.34, "resistance_profile_alignment": "poor", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mid_range"}, {"H_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "deltoid_lateral", "etu_cm2": 7.60, "rationale": "Part dynamic contribution to horizontal abduction, part isometric support of the abducted arm. Slightly below reference because only the posterior portion of the head is meaningfully loaded and its excursion is small.", "normalized_etu": 0.1662, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric", "isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "limited", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 45.73, "smh_interpretation": 