"elbow_joint", "rationale": "The elbow flexors must generate substantial force to elevate the heavily loaded body against gravity. Brachialis, brachioradialis, and biceps brachii contribute strongly in the neutral-grip configuration, producing high elbow-joint reaction and compression. Exposure is high but remains below the most localized heavy curling patterns because shoulder and scapular musculature share a large fraction of the total pulling demand.", "load_exposure": 0.7000, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "scapulothoracic_articulation", "rationale": "The scapulae must move from an elevated and upwardly rotated position toward depression and downward rotation while transmitting the approximately 100 kg system load between the upper limbs and thorax. Trapezial, rhomboid, serratus, and associated scapular musculature generate substantial force and must coordinate freely throughout the pull. Added external loading increases force transmission relative to an unweighted pull-up, producing high functional scapulothoracic exposure.", "load_exposure": 0.6600, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "muscle_force_transmission", "rotation", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "high", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "acromioclavicular_joint", "rationale": "The AC joint transmits substantial force through the shoulder girdle while the scapula moves through elevation, depression, and rotation under a heavily loaded vertical pulling task. The neutral grip avoids some of the more constrained shoulder positioning of a wide pronated pull-up, but the added load preserves meaningful AC-joint force transmission and rotational demand.", "load_exposure": 0.3600, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission", "rotation", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "moderate", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "moderate", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "radiocarpal_joint", "rationale": "The wrists remain approximately neutral while the hands transmit the full system load through the handles. Finger-flexor and forearm forces generate meaningful radiocarpal force transmission, but direct wrist flexion-extension torque remains limited, so exposure stays low despite very high grip demand.", "load_exposure": 0.1800, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "glenohumeral_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
