lly rotated lower position, but the arm remains anterior to the torso and does not create a pronounced loaded stretch.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 6.32, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "shortened"}, {"H_m": 0.9000, "muscle": "trapezius_lower", "etu_cm2": 3.45, "rationale": "Mixed dynamic and stabilizing scapular tension is meaningful but slightly below conventional reference-quality loading.", "normalized_etu": 0.2303, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric", "isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "limited", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 14.98, "smh_interpretation": "The lower trapezius dynamically assists scapular rotation and tilt but also performs substantial fixation with limited isolated excursion.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.83, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "wrist_flexors", "etu_cm2": 2.55, "rationale": "Grip tension is mechanically meaningful but predominantly isometric and low-ROM.", "normalized_etu": 0.0469, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "smh_interpretation": "The grip remains nearly fixed while the dumbbells rotate and move overhead, producing sustained force without productive wrist or finger excursion.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "wrist_extensors", "etu_cm2": 1.70, "rationale": "The exposure supports wrist stability but remains predominantly isometric and accessory.", "normalized_etu": 0.0317, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.67, "smh_interpretation": "The wrist extensors stabilize the hand beneath the dumbbell without meaningful dynamic wrist extension.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "trapezius_middle", "etu_cm2": 1.70, "rationale": "The muscle performs meaningful but predominantly stabilizing and braking tension through limited productive ROM.", "normalized_etu": 0.0649, "contraction_mode": ["isometric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 26.18, "smh_interpretation": "The middle trapezius regulates scapular protraction but does not perform broad loaded retraction.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "obliques", "etu_cm2": 1.70, "rationale": "Low-level anti-rotation tension is mechanically specific but predominantly isometric and low-ROM.", "normalized_etu": 0.0208, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "smh_interpretation": "The trunk remains nearly fixed while the obliques resist small rotational and lateral disturbances.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "pectoralis_minor", "etu_cm2": 1.28, "rationale": "Predominantly isometric scapular-control tension warrants a below-reference modifier.", "normalized_etu": 0.1184, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 10.81, "smh_interpretation": "The muscle provides minor scapular fixation rather than broad dynamic protraction or depression.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "pronators_supinators", "etu_cm2": 1.28, "rationale": "Rotational control is mechanically meaningful but remains low-load, accessory, and largely isometric.", "normalized_etu": 0.0210, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "limited", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 60.88, "smh_interpretation": "The group controls forearm rotation, but the movement is not a directly resisted full-ROM pronation or supination exercise.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8000, "muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "etu_cm2": 1.20, "rationale": "Low-ROM postural bracing represents distinctly lower hypertrophic tension quality than conventional dynamic loading.", "normalized_etu": 0.0546, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "smh_interpretation": "The muscle provides low-level circumferential bracing without productive excursion, while the seat and backrest supply substantial external support.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "poor", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "moderate", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}], "modifier_distribution": {"mode": 0.8500, "median": 0.9000, "maximum": 1.1000, "minimum": 0.8000, "unweighted_mean": 0.9118, "tension_weighted_mean": 0.9656}, "hypertrophic_quality_ratio": 0.9656, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 148.17}	{"obliques": 0.9500, "rotator_cuffs": 1.0000, "wrist_flexors": 0.9500, "deltoid_lateral": 1.0000, "trapezius_lower": 1.0000, "trapezius_upper": 1.0000, "wrist_extensors": 0.9500, "deltoid_anterior": 1.0000, "pectoralis_minor": 0.9500, "trapezius_middle": 0.9500, "serratus_anterior": 1.0000, "triceps_long_head": 1.0000, "triceps_medial_head": 1.0000, "pronators_supinators": 0.9500, "transverse_abdominis": 0.9500, "triceps_lateral_head": 1.0000, "pectoralis_major_clavicular": 1.0000}	{"slug": "seated_dumbbell_arnold_press", "notes": ["No muscle warranted an above-reference value: the rotational start position is a shortened rather than lengthened position for the deltoids and pectoral fibres, so the exercise's extended path increases tension exposure without creating lengthened-position loading.", "This matches the conventional dumbbell overhead press evaluation, where the same absence of a loaded stretch produced a uniform reference for the prime movers.", "Rotator cuffs sit at the reference and were explicitly treated as dynamic agonists here, since the Arnold press is defined by loaded external rotation that the cuff drives directly — but the low tension fraction and controlled rotation give no basis for elevation.", "The long head of triceps was held at the reference because its elbow and shoulder actions offset in this pattern, unlike the California press where the forehead-directed bar path makes them compound.", "The rotational component was treated as an extended movement path, not as rapid force development; a standardized repetition specifies controlled conventional tempo throughout."], "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "deltoid_anterior", "rationale": "The rotational start position has the humerus adducted and internally rotated in front of the body, which is a shortened rather than lengthened position for the anterior deltoid — it is shortest at both the bottom and near lockout. The extended rotational path prolongs meaningful tension somewhat, but with no lengthened-position loading and no eccentric emphasis, the neutral reference is appropriate. The high tension fraction reflects load magnitude already carried by T_m.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 30.46, "tension_fraction": 0.7797, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 23.75, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "prolonged", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["conventional_contractile_fatigue"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "triceps_lateral_head", "rationale": "Conventional dynamic elbow extension; the monoarticular lateral head is unaffected by the rotational shoulder component and never reaches an unusually lengthened position. No structural mechanism accompanies the high tension fraction.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.10, "tension_fraction": 0.6396, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 23.09, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["conventional_contractile_fatigue"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "deltoid_lateral", "rationale": "The rotation sweeps it through a longer arc than a conventional press, which is reflected in its tension exposure, but the muscle is at moderate rather than extreme length at the adducted start and no high-force lengthening occurs. Conventional dynamic tension applies.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 45.73, "tension_fraction": 0.4028, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "substantial", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 18.42, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "prolonged", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["conventional_contractile_fatigue"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "triceps_long_head", "rationale": "Its distal lengthening from elbow flexion at the bottom is offset by the shoulder being flexed and adducted in the start position, so the two joint actions do not compound into a lengthened-position load — unlike the California press where they do.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 43.55, "tension_fraction": 0.3796, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "moderate", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 16.53, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["conventional_contractile_fatigue"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "serratus_anterior", "rationale": "Overhead pressing requires genuine dynamic upward scapular rotation through the full range rather than static positional holding, so this is conventional dynamic contraction with a controlled eccentric at the reference value.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.03, "tension_fraction": 0.4394, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "substantial", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 15.83, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["conventional_contractile_fatigue"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "The Arnold press makes the cuff a genuine dynamic agonist rather than a stabilizer: the movement is defined by loaded humeral external rotation through the ascent, which the cuff drives directly. Free dumbbells also require active head control through an unguided arc. This places it at the reference rather than the sub-reference stabilizer value, though the low tension fraction and controlled rotation give no basis for elevation.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "tension_fraction": 0.0586, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 10.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "prolonged", "sustained_