 "high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "moderate", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "scapulothoracic_articulation", "rationale": "The scapulae retract and remain controlled against the thorax while substantial dumbbell forces are transferred from the arms into the supported trunk. Middle trapezius, rhomboids, serratus anterior, and other scapular stabilizers generate substantial force throughout the rowing motion. Chest support reduces whole-body stabilization but preserves strong local scapular retraction and fixation demands.", "load_exposure": 0.6000, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "elbow_joint", "rationale": "The elbow flexors generate substantial force to overcome the external extension moment created by the dumbbells. Brachialis, brachioradialis, and biceps contribute meaningful joint reaction and compression. Exposure is substantial but remains below direct curling exercises because shoulder and scapular musculature share a large fraction of the total pulling demand.", "load_exposure": 0.5800, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "radiocarpal_joint", "rationale": "The wrists remain near neutral while transmitting grip force to the dumbbells. Forearm musculature must maintain wrist position under substantial load, producing meaningful radiocarpal force transmission, but direct wrist flexion-extension moment remains modest.", "load_exposure": 0.1800, "loaded_joint_position": 