ric lengthening as the arm returns forward. The long-length component is only mild in this row configuration, supporting a small recovery premium.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 4.50, "tension_fraction": 0.5222, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "substantial", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.35, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["substantial_relative_tension", "controlled_dynamic_shoulder_extension"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "mild"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "Oblique exposure is minimal relative to available FCSA and consists primarily of trunk stabilization. No meaningful persistent structural recovery mechanism is present.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "tension_fraction": 0.0245, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["trunk_stabilization"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "trapezius_upper", "rationale": "Upper-trapezius involvement is low-relative-load scapular stabilization without unusual eccentric or high-force lengthened loading.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 19.36, "tension_fraction": 0.0775, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["scapular_position_stabilization"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "rationale": "Rectus-abdominis activity is low-relative-load trunk bracing against cable-induced torso motion. The exposure lacks meaningful structural stress and is unlikely to leave substantial persistent local force impairment.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "tension_fraction": 0.0618, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["trunk_bracing"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "serratus_anterior", "rationale": "Serratus-anterior involvement is low and primarily contributes to scapular control during the rowing cycle. No strong persistent recovery-cost mechanism is present.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.03, "tension_fraction": 0.0416, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["scapular_control"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "pronators_supinators", "rationale": "Pronator-supinator exposure is minimal relative to available capacity and serves predominantly to maintain forearm orientation against the cable handle.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 60.88, "tension_fraction": 0.0197, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.20, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["forearm_orientation_stabilization"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "rationale": "Transverse-abdominal exposure is low-relative-load bracing without meaningful dynamic structural loading or sustained high-force perfusion restriction.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "tension_fraction": 0.0546, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.20, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["abdominal_bracing"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}], "modifier_distribution": {"mode": 0.9500, "median": 0.9500, "maximum": 1.1000, "minimum": 0.9500, "unweighted_mean": 0.9947, "tension_weighted_mean": 1.0255}, "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}, "active_tension_exposure_sum_cm2": 193.37}	{"elbow_joint": 0.6000, "lumbar_spine": 0.1200, "radiocarpal_joint": 0.1600, "glenohumeral_joint": 0.7000, "acromioclavicular_joint": 0.2200, "scapulothoracic_articulation": 0.6200}	{"slug": "wide_grip_seated_cable_row", "notes": ["The wide grip shifts the exercise toward greater shoulder horizontal-abduction and scapular-retraction demand relative to narrower neutral-grip cable rows.", "Elbow exposure remains substantial but is relatively less dominant because the wide-arm geometry increases the contribution of posterior shoulder and scapular musculature.", "Seated cable execution keeps lumbar exposure low provided the repetition is performed without deliberate torso momentum."], "loaded_joints": ["glenohumeral_joint", "scapulothoracic_articulation", "elbow_joint", "acromioclavicular_joint", "radiocarpal_joint", "lumbar_spine"], "reconciliation": "PASS", "joint_evaluation": [{"joint": "glenohumeral_joint", "rationale": "The glenohumeral joint is a primary loaded articulation. The 80 kg cable resistance creates substantial shoulder-flexion and horizontal-adduction moments that must be opposed during shoulder extension and horizontal abduction. The wide grip increases the horizontal-abduction component and keeps the humeri farther from the torso, increasing posterior-deltoid, rotator-cuff, and associated shoulder-force demand. High muscle force produces meaningful glenohumeral compression and translational control, while the cable path provides more external constraint than free dumbbells or a barbell.", "load_exposure": 0.7000, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "translation", "muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "moderate", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "scapulothoracic_articulation", "rationale": "The wide-grip row requires substantial scapular retraction and controlled protraction through the return phase. Middle trapezius, rhomboids, posterior shoulder musculature, and associated scapular stabilizers transmit large cable forces between the upper limbs and thorax. The wide grip emphasizes scapular retraction mechanics relative to narrower rowing variants, producing substantial functional scapulothoracic exposure.", "load_exposure": 0.6200, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "elbow_joint", "rationale": "The elbow flexors must overcome a substantial external extension moment as the cable is pulled toward the torso. Brachialis, brachioradialis, and biceps generate meaningful joint reaction and compression. Exposure remains substantial but is somewhat lower than in narrower neutral-grip rows or direct curls because the wide grip shifts a larger share of the pulling task toward shoulder horizontal abduction and scapular retraction.", "load_exposure": 0.6000, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "acromioclavicular_joint", "rationale": "Substantial scapular retraction under cable resistance requires force transmission through the scapula-clavicle interface. This creates meaningful but secondary AC-joint exposure, without the high elevation, compression, or overhead rotational demand seen in pressing and overhead-loading exercises.", "load_exposure": 0.2200, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "radiocarpal_joint", "rationale": "The wrists mainly transmit grip force while remaining approximately neutral on the wide handle. Forearm musculature must stabilize the hands against substantial cable tension, but direct wrist flexion-extension or deviation moment remains limited.", "load_exposure": 0.1600, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "lumbar_spine", "rationale": "The seated position substantially reduces lower-body and spinal loading compared with unsupported rows. The lumbar spine still provides isometric trunk stabilization against the horizontal cable force, but with technically valid execution and limited torso swing the external trunk moment remains small.", "load_exposure": 0.1200, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["stabilization", "compression"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "glenohumeral_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
standing_dumbbell_shrug	80.00	111.06	{"obliques": 2.45, "rhomboids": 14.13, "rotator_cuffs": 5.98, "wrist_flexors": 32.10, "erector_spinae": 12.78, "trapezius_lower": 3.15, "trapezius_upper": 17.42, "trapezius_middle": 13.09, "deep_neck_extensors": 8.49, "transverse_abdominis": 1.47}	{"soleus": 1.50, "obliques": 2.70, "rhomboids": 14.80, "rotator_cuffs": 6.50, "wrist_flexors": 33.00, "erector_spinae": 13.50, "gluteus_medius": 2.00, "trapezius_lower": 3.50, "trapezius_upper": 18.20, "wrist_extensors": 3.50, "rectus_abdominis": 1.50, "trapezius_middle": 13.70, "serratus_anterior": 1.50, "deep_neck_extensors": 8.49, "pronators_supinators": 1.20, "transverse_abdominis": 1.70}	{"slug": "standing_dumbbell_shrug", "notes": ["The supplied contribution vector sums exactly to the systemic propulsive FCSA demand.", "The supplied wrist-flexor, erector-spinae, deep-neck-extensor, cuff, oblique, and transverse-abdominis values were interpreted primarily as grip, load-transmission, and postural stabilization exposure.", "The upper trapezius is the principal dynamic mover, while the rhomboids and middle and lower trapezius provide mixed scapular-control roles.", "Additional exposure was limited to antagonist wrist fixation, forearm orientation, complementary scapular control, abdominal co-contraction, and standing postural stabilization.", "The repetition is modeled without deliberate elbow flexion, spinal extension, knee drive, or rolling of the shoulders."], "added_muscles": ["wrist_extensors", "gluteus_medius", "serratus_anterior", "soleus", "rectus_abdominis", "pronators_supinators"], "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Maintains the dumbbell grip and transmits the full implement load through the hands throughout the set. A small increment reflects sustained grip tension during both elevation and controlled lowering.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "mechanical_roles": ["grip_maintenance", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.6066, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 32.10, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 33.00, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "trapezius_upper", "rationale": "Produces the dominant scapular-elevation torque and eccentrically controls depression under the dumbbell load. A modest increment reflects continuous clavicular and superior-scapular stabilization accompanying the dynamic shrug.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 19.36, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "scapular_control", "eccentric_control", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.9401, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 17.42, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric", "isometric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 18.20, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "rhomboids", "rationale": "Maintains medial scapular alignment and limits excessive protraction or rotation while the shoulder girdle elevates. A small increment reflects continuous scapular fixation beyond the supplied mixed contribution.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 28.25, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation", "multi_joint_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.5239, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 14.13, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile", "dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 14.80, "input_contribution_classification": "mixed_propulsive_and_stabilizing"}, {"muscle": "trapezius_middle", "rationale": "Stabilizes the scapulae against anterior displacement and regulates their orientation during elevation and depression. A modest increment represents continuous medial stabilization.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 26.18, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation", "multi_joint_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.5233, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 13.09, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile", "dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 13.70, "input_contribution_classification": "mixed_propulsive_and_stabilizing"}, {"muscle": "erector_spinae", "rationale": "Maintains upright spinal alignment while the heavy dumbbells create sustained axial and anterior-posterior perturbations. A small increment reflects continuous anti-flexion tension.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 106.48, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "isometric_fixation", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.1268, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 12.78, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 13.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "deep_neck_extensors", "rationale": "Maintains neutral cervical alignment as the shoulder girdle elevates beneath the head. The supplied contribution is retained as the complete cervical-position demand.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 84.88, "mechanical_roles": ["isometric_fixation", "limb_position_maintenance", "load_transmission"], "tension_fraction": 0.1000, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 8.49, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 8.49, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "Centres the humeral heads while the arms act as suspended load-transmission links beneath the dumbbells. A small increment reflects continuous glenohumeral stabilization.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 170.80, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "load_transmission", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0381, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 5.98, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 6.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "trapezius_lower", "rationale": "Regulates excessive scapular elevation and anterior tilt while contributing to controlled depression during the eccentric return. A small increment reflects this antagonist and stabilizing role.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 14.98, "mechanical_roles": ["scapular_control", "antagonist_co_contraction", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.2336, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 3.15, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "wrist_extensors", "rationale": "Co-contracts with the wrist flexors to maintain neutral wrist alignment beneath the heavy dumbbells.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.67, "mechanical_roles": ["grip_maintenance", "antagonist_co_contraction", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0652, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 3.50, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "Resists lateral trunk deviation and rotation caused by independently suspended dumbbells. A minimal increment reflects continuous bilateral anti-rotation tension.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "mechanical_roles": ["trunk_bracing", "antagonist_co_contraction", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0330, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 2.45, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.70, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_stabilizing_or_load_transmitting"}, {"muscle": "gluteus_medius", "rationale": "Maintains frontal-plane pelvic stability while the athlete stands under bilateral external load.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 113.75, "mechanical_roles": ["joint_stabilization", "limb_position_maintenance", "isometric_fixation"], "tension_fraction": 0.0176, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 0.00, "contraction_character": ["isometric", "co_contractile"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "input_contri