 exercises acting on the ankle, a heavy standing calf raise is near the upper end of mechanical exposure.", "load_exposure": 0.9000, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "muscle_force_transmission", "loaded_end_range"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "very_high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "very_high"}, {"joint": "tibiofemoral_joint", "rationale": "The knees remain nearly extended while large axial forces are transmitted through the lower limbs. Gastrocnemius force crosses the knee and the quadriceps and hamstrings provide modest isometric stabilization, creating some tibiofemoral compression. However, direct knee flexion-extension moment and knee motion remain small, so exposure is low relative to exercises that directly load the knee.", "load_exposure": 0.1400, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["compression", "muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "hip_joint", "rationale": "The hip mainly transmits axial load while maintaining an upright standing position. Smith-machine guidance substantially reduces balance and frontal-plane stabilization requirements, and there is little meaningful hip motion or external hip moment.", "load_exposure": 0.0800, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["axial_loading", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "minimal", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "talocrural_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
plate_loaded_converging_incline_chest_press	70.00	141.68	{"rotator_cuffs": 6.32, "deltoid_lateral": 3.90, "deltoid_anterior": 23.14, "pectoralis_minor": 0.96, "serratus_anterior": 6.12, "triceps_long_head": 21.53, "triceps_medial_head": 11.46, "triceps_lateral_head": 26.53, "pectoralis_major_sternal": 31.90, "pectoralis_major_clavicular": 9.82}	{"obliques": 2.00, "rhomboids": 3.50, "rotator_cuffs": 8.00, "wrist_flexors": 5.00, "erector_spinae": 3.00, "deltoid_lateral": 3.90, "trapezius_lower": 2.50, "deltoid_anterior": 23.14, "latissimus_dorsi": 2.00, "pectoralis_minor": 0.96, "trapezius_middle": 3.50, "serratus_anterior": 6.12, "triceps_long_head": 21.53, "triceps_medial_head": 11.46, "transverse_abdominis": 1.50, "triceps_lateral_head": 26.53, "pectoralis_major_sternal": 31.90, "pectoralis_major_clavicular": 9.82}	{"slug": "plate_loaded_converging_incline_chest_press", "notes": ["Supplied vector sums to 141.68, matching systemic_propulsive_fcsa_demand exactly.", "rotator_cuffs is the only supplied value increased, from 6.32 to 8.00, and the increase is deliberately smaller than the equivalent adjustment in the barbell bench press. A fixed converging path constrains the handles in every plane except the intended one, which removes most of the humeral restraint demand a free bar creates.", "Tension expansion ratio of 1.1742 is among the lowest in this series and sits well below the barbell bench press at 1.2229 and the dumbbell overhead press at 1.3865. This is the expected ordering: a seated plate-loaded machine with a guided path externalizes far more stabilization than either free-weight alternative.", "The internal distribution of the supplied vector is mechanically coherent for an incline. pectoralis_major_clavicular reaches a 0.7263 tension fraction here against 0.5850 on the flat bench, while pectoralis_major_sternal falls from 0.8220 to 0.5965. The inclined path shifts share toward the upper fibres and the anterior deltoid.", "pectoralis_minor was supplied but cannot be propulsive, since it has no humeral attachment. Retained at its supplied value as the mandated lower bound and reclassified.", "gluteus_maximus was excluded here despite being included in the barbell bench press. No leg drive or arch maintenance is required in a seated machine press, so no specific mechanical pathway justifies hip extensor tension.", "rectus_abdominis was excluded, as the inclined seat holds the trunk and no lumbar extension moment requires active anterior resistance."], "added_muscles": ["wrist_flexors", "trapezius_middle", "rhomboids", "erector_spinae", "trapezius_lower", "obliques", "latissimus_dorsi", "transverse_abdominis"], "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"muscle": "pectoralis_major_sternal", "rationale": "Generates horizontal adduction torque against the handles. Its value sits below the flat bench figure, consistent with the inclined path shifting share toward the clavicular fibres and anterior deltoid. Supplied value retained.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.48, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.5965, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 31.90, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 31.90, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "triceps_lateral_head", "rationale": "Elbow extension torque through the pressing arc. Supplied value retained; the machine imposes no separate stabilizing demand on this muscle.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.10, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.7349, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 26.53, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 26.53, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "deltoid_anterior", "rationale": "Co-prime mover for humeral flexion, with a larger share than on a flat bench because the inclined press path aligns more closely with its line of action. Supplied value retained.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 30.46, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.7597, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 23.14, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 23.14, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "triceps_long_head", "rationale": "Contributes elbow extension while spanning the shoulder, where it also resists the flexion moment. One force state serving both joints; supplied value retained.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 43.55, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "multi_joint_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.4944, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 21.53, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 21.53, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "triceps_medial_head", "rationale": "Monoarticular elbow extensor active across the full extension range. Supplied value retained.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 15.59, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.7351, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 11.46, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 11.46, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "pectoralis_major_clavicular", "rationale": "The inclined path matches the upward and inward fibre direction of the clavicular head, which explains its markedly higher value than on the flat bench. Supplied value retained.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 13.52, "mechanical_roles": ["propulsive", "eccentric_control"], "tension_fraction": 0.7263, "propulsive_fcsa_cm2": 9.82, "contraction_character": ["dynamic_concentric", "dynamic_eccentric"], "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 9.82, "input_contribution_classification": "primarily_propulsive"}, {"muscle": "rotator_cuffs", "rationale": "Increased modestly from 6.32 to 8.00. Humeral head centring is required against 