rting a near-reference modifier.", "normalized_etu": 0.6662, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric", "isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 14.98, "smh_interpretation": "The lower trapezius dynamically controls scapular depression, tilt, and rotation but also bears a substantial isometric fixation role.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 10.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "etu_cm2": 5.10, "rationale": "Sustained anti-extension tension is mechanically meaningful but predominantly isometric and low-ROM.", "normalized_etu": 0.2100, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "smh_interpretation": "The trunk remains rigid while the rectus abdominis resists lumbar extension and body swing without meaningful spinal-flexion excursion.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 6.00, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.8500, "muscle": "obliques", "etu_cm2": 4.68, "rationale": "Anti-rotation bracing is mechanically specific but lacks productive dynamic excursion.", "normalized_etu": 0.0573, "contraction_mode": ["isometric"], "high_tension_rom": "brief", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "smh_interpretation": "The obliques prevent rotation and lateral deviation while the trunk remains nearly fixed.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 5.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "moderate", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "mixed"}, {"H_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "brachioradialis", "etu_cm2": 4.28, "rationale": "Useful dynamic loading from an extended elbow is moderated by nonoptimal forearm orientation.", "normalized_etu": 0.3815, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maxim