ctive-tension magnitude.", "The lateral deltoid and serratus anterior receive modest reductions because their roles are secondary or mixed with stabilization.", "Cuff, grip, wrist, scapular-stabilizer, and trunk contributions receive reduced modifiers because their exposure is predominantly isometric, co-contractile, or limited in productive ROM.", "ETU values equal active tension exposure multiplied by the listed H_m values within rounding tolerance."], "etu_sum_cm2": 167.13, "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"H_m": 1.0500, "muscle": "pectoralis_major_sternal", "etu_cm2": 35.42, "rationale": "Stable machine execution, controlled eccentric loading, and meaningful tension in the lengthened lower position support a modest positive modifier despite the incline reducing direct sternal alignment.", "normalized_etu": 0.6622, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "broad", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.48, "smh_interpretation": "The lower position places the sternal fibres under useful stretch while the guided bar preserves continuous pressing tension through a broad shoulder and elbow ROM.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 33.73, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "triceps_lateral_head", "etu_cm2": 28.40, "rationale": "The lateral head receives high conventional concentric and eccentric elbow-extension tension through substantial ROM without an exceptional muscle-specific advantage.", "normalized_etu": 0.7867, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.10, "smh_interpretation": "The elbow begins substantially flexed and moves through a large extension range under stable external resistance.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 28.40, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "deltoid_anterior", "etu_cm2": 25.29, "rationale": "The exercise provides high-quality dynamic anterior-deltoid tension, but the muscle's very high recruitment and stable path are already represented by exposure magnitude and do not independently require a bonus.", "normalized_etu": 0.8303, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "broad", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 30.46, "smh_interpretation": "The inclined path aligns strongly with shoulder flexion and loads the anterior deltoid through a broad range, including controlled tension in the extended lower position.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 25.29, "resistance_profile_alignment": "very_good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "moderately_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 1.0500, "muscle": "triceps_long_head", "etu_cm2": 24.68, "rationale": "Combined shoulder flexion and elbow flexion create meaningful long-length triceps tension, supporting a modest bonus without equating the press to a dedicated overhead extension.", "normalized_etu": 0.5667, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 43.55, "smh_interpretation": "The flexed shoulder position lengthens the biarticular long head proximally while elbow flexion lengthens it distally during the lower phase.", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 23.50, "resistance_profile_alignment": "good", "duration_of_meaningful_tension": "sustained", "muscle_length_under_high_tension": "substantially_lengthened"}, {"H_m": 1.0000, "muscle": "triceps_medial_head", "etu_cm2": 12.26, "rationale": "High conventional concentric and eccentric elbow-extension loading through substantial ROM represents the neutral dynamic reference.", "normalized_etu": 0.7864, "contraction_mode": ["concentric", "eccentric"], "high_tension_rom": "substantial", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 15.59, "smh_interpretation": "The medial h