al active tension persists during controlled eccentric loading into relatively lengthened positions.", "Anterior deltoid and the monoarticular triceps heads receive only mild elevations because their primary distinguishing feature is high or very high relative tension rather than unusual structural loading.", "The Smith-machine constraint does not itself increase muscle recovery cost; it primarily reduces stabilization requirements relative to a free-weight press.", "Low-level shoulder, scapular, wrist, and trunk stabilizers are assigned slightly sub-reference modifiers where their exposure lacks a strong persistent recovery mechanism.", "No eccentric overload, exaggerated tempo, runtime volume effect, RIR effect, novelty effect, hypertrophy-specific factor, joint cost, tendon cost, systemic fatigue, or neural recovery cost was incorporated."], "reconciliation": "PASS", "muscle_evaluation": [{"R_m": 1.1000, "muscle": "pectoralis_major_sternal", "rationale": "The sternal pectoralis bears high relative tension and remains meaningfully active during the controlled eccentric descent into shoulder horizontal abduction and extension relative to the pressing position. This produces a clear but conventional loaded-lengthening recovery premium.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.48, "tension_fraction": 0.6307, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "high", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 33.73, "eccentric_structural_stress": "standard", "meaningful_tension_duration": "reference", "sustained_isometric_tension": "none", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["high_relative_tension", "loaded_lengthening_during_press_descent", "conventional_contractile_fatigue"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "moderate"}, {"R_m": 1.0500, "muscle": "triceps_lateral_head", "rationale": "The lateral head operates at a high fraction of available FCSA, but its concentric and eccentric elbow-extension mechanics remain conventional. The nonlinea