anterior activity is low relative to available capacity and mainly maintains scapular position for the overhead arm posture. There is no unusual eccentric or high-force long-length loading.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 36.03, "tension_fraction": 0.0694, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "moderate", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["scapular_upward_rotation_and_position_stabilization"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "obliques", "rationale": "Oblique involvement is very low relative to available FCSA and consists primarily of trunk stabilization against the cable force. Persistent local recovery burden per unit tension is slightly below conventional dynamic loading.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 81.71, "tension_fraction": 0.0245, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["trunk_stabilization"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "wrist_flexors", "rationale": "Wrist-flexor tension is very low and primarily serves rope grip and wrist stabilization. No meaningful structural or persistent metabolic recovery mechanism is present.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 54.40, "tension_fraction": 0.0368, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 2.00, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["rope_grip_stabilization"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "wrist_extensors", "rationale": "Wrist-extensor activity is very low-relative-load stabilization without relevant eccentric structural stress or prolonged high-force occlusion.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 53.67, "tension_fraction": 0.0279, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["wrist_stabilization"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "rectus_abdominis", "rationale": "Rectus-abdominis exposure is low and consists of anti-extension bracing against the cable's tendency to alter trunk position. The force level is insufficient to imply meaningful persistent local recovery debt.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 24.29, "tension_fraction": 0.0618, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_tension": "intermittent", "dominant_recovery_mechanisms": ["anti_extension_trunk_stabilization"], "high_force_lengthening_at_long_length": "none"}, {"R_m": 0.9500, "muscle": "transverse_abdominis", "rationale": "Transverse-abdominal activity is low-relative-load bracing without dynamic structural loading. Its persistent recovery burden per unit tension is therefore slightly below reference.", "maximum_fcsa_cm2": 21.97, "tension_fraction": 0.0683, "perfusion_constraint": "low", "force_development_profile": "controlled", "relative_tension_severity": "low", "active_tension_exposure_cm2": 1.50, "eccentric_structural_stress": "minimal", "meaningful_tension_duration": "continuous", "sustained_isometric_t