it remains mechanically relevant in either case."], "loaded_joints": ["glenohumeral_joint", "elbow_joint", "scapulothoracic_articulation", "acromioclavicular_joint", "radiocarpal_joint"], "reconciliation": "PASS", "joint_evaluation": [{"joint": "glenohumeral_joint", "rationale": "The glenohumeral joint is the primary loaded articulation. The 80 kg plate-loaded resistance creates a large external horizontal-abduction and extension moment that must be opposed by pectoralis major, anterior deltoid, and associated shoulder musculature during horizontal pressing. High agonist and rotator-cuff force produces substantial glenohumeral compression and translational control demand, especially in the deeper portion of the press where the humerus is more horizontally abducted. The machine constrains the resistance path and reduces stabilization requirements relative to a free barbell or dumbbells, but local shoulder moment and muscle-force transmission remain high.", "load_exposure": 0.7600, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "translation", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "moderate", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "very_high"}, {"joint": "elbow_joint", "rationale": "The elbow undergoes substantial extension against the machine resistance. Triceps force opposes the external elbow-flexion moment and produces meaningful elbow-joint reaction and compression. Exposure is substantial but lower than in direct heavy elbow-extension exercises because the pressing task is shared with the shoulder.", "load_exposure": 0.6500, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["net_joint_moment", "compression", "muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "high", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "high"}, {"joint": "scapulothoracic_articulation", "rationale": "The scapulae must remain mechanically controlled against the thorax while transmitting pressing forces between the upper limbs and trunk. Depending on machine design, some protraction may occur near terminal reach, while serratus anterior and trapezial musculature maintain scapular position throughout the press. The supported torso and guided handles reduce stabilization demand relative to free-weight pressing, but scapulothoracic force transmission remains meaningful.", "load_exposure": 0.4600, "loaded_joint_position": "mid_range", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization", "net_joint_moment"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "moderate", "stabilization_requirement": "moderate", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "acromioclavicular_joint", "rationale": "Pressing force is transmitted through the scapula-clavicle complex while the shoulder girdle is loaded in horizontal pressing. This produces meaningful AC-joint compression and force transmission, particularly in the deeper portion of the movement, but the guided machine and supported torso keep exposure below heavy free-weight or overhead pressing patterns.", "load_exposure": 0.4000, "loaded_joint_position": "demanding", "primary_loading_modes": ["compression", "muscle_force_transmission", "stabilization"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "moderate", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "low", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "moderate"}, {"joint": "radiocarpal_joint", "rationale": "The wrist primarily transmits handle force while remaining close to neutral. The machine handles reduce the need for significant wrist stabilization or direct flexion-extension torque, so radiocarpal exposure remains low.", "load_exposure": 0.1200, "loaded_joint_position": "favorable", "primary_loading_modes": ["muscle_force_transmission"], "net_joint_moment_demand": "low", "stabilization_requirement": "low", "shear_translation_or_rotation": "minimal", "muscle_force_and_joint_reaction": "low"}], "maximum_exposure_joint": "glenohumeral_joint", "standardized_repetition": {"tempo": "controlled conventional tempo", "range_of_motion": "full intended ROM", "proximity_to_failure": "effective repetition"}}
